{"path":"numeric/bit_width","title":"std::bit_width","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>bit_width","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/bit_width","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"If x is not zero, calculates the number of bits needed to store the value x, that is, 1 + floor(log2(x)). If x is zero, returns zero.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/bit\">&lt;bit&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> bit_width<span class=\"br0\">(</span> T x <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code> is not zero, calculates the number of bits needed to store the value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code>, that is, <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"1 + \\lfloor \\log_2(x) \\rfloor\">1 + floor(log<span class=\"t-su t-su-b\">2</span>(x))</span>. If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code> is zero, returns zero.\n</p><p>This overload participates in overload resolution only if <code>T</code> is an unsigned integer type (that is, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span></span>, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">short</span></span>, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">int</span></span>, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span></span>, <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span> <span class=\"kw4\">long</span></span>, or an extended unsigned integer type).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> x\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> unsigned integer value\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Zero if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code> is zero; otherwise, one plus the base-2 logarithm of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code>, with any fractional part discarded.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This function is equivalent to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">digits</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/countl_zero\"><span class=\"kw1568\">std::<span class=\"me2\">countl_zero</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>x<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable ftm-begin ftm-has-value\">\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/feature_test\">Feature-test</a> macro</th>\n<th><abbr>Value</abbr></th>\n<th><abbr>Std</abbr></th>\n<th>Feature\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_int_pow2\"><code>__cpp_lib_int_pow2</code></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/compiler_support/20#cpp_lib_int_pow2_202002L\"><code>202002L</code></a></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark\">(C++20)</span></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric#Bit_manipulation_.28since_C.2B.2B20.29\">Integral power-of-2 operations</a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;bit&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;bitset&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> x<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> x <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu8\">010</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>x<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"bit_width( \"</span>\n                  <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/bitset\"><span class=\"kw1034\">std::<span class=\"me2\">bitset</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nu0\">4</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">{</span>x<span class=\"br0\">}</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" ) = \"</span>\n                  <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">bit_width</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>x<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>bit_width( 0000 ) = 0\nbit_width( 0001 ) = 1\nbit_width( 0010 ) = 2\nbit_width( 0011 ) = 2\nbit_width( 0100 ) = 3\nbit_width( 0101 ) = 3\nbit_width( 0110 ) = 3\nbit_width( 0111 ) = 3</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue3656\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 3656</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++20\n</td>\n<td>the return type of <code>bit_width</code> is the same as the type of its function argument\n</td>\n<td>made it <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span></span>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/countl_zero\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>countl_zero</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  counts the number of consecutive <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code> bits, starting from the most significant bit <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::bit_width","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. If x is not zero, calculates the number of bits needed to store the value x, that is, 1 + floor(log2(x))."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"x"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Zero if x is zero; otherwise, one plus the base-2 logarithm of x, with any fractional part discarded."},{"label":"Notes","note":"This function is equivalent to return std::numeric_limits<T>::digits - std::countl_zero(x);."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"countl_zero","note":"counts the number of consecutive 0 bits, starting from the most significant bit"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":259,"codeBlockCount":2}
